\name{cellucid_field_summary}
\alias{cellucid_field_summary}
\title{Summarize a field per category}
\usage{
cellucid_field_summary(
  viewer,
  field,
  by,
  categories,
  top = 50,
  visible_only = FALSE,
  within
)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{field}{A field by name: source "obs" for a column of the cells, "var" for a gene; key is the name as shown. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{key}}{The field or gene name as the app shows it. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{source}}{"obs" for a column of the cells, "var" for a gene. One of \code{"obs"}, \code{"var"}. Required.}}}
\item{by}{The categorical obs field to group the cells by. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{key}}{The field or gene name as the app shows it. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{source}}{"obs" for a column of the cells, "var" for a gene. One of \code{"obs"}, \code{"var"}. Required.}}}
\item{categories}{Only these categories of \code{by}, by name (else every category with cells). A vector or list of text (at least 1 character) (at least 1 item, each once). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{top}{For a categorical field: at most this many of its categories per group. A whole number (at least 1). Default \code{50}, the viewer's own.}
\item{visible_only}{Only the cells the active view shows. \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{FALSE}, the viewer's own.}
\item{within}{Only the cells of some categories of another categorical field, or in a range of a continuous field or gene (both ends included), leaving the view as it is: donors within one cell type, cell types per age range. A named list. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does). \describe{\item{\code{categories}}{For a categorical field: its categories, by name. A vector or list of text (at least 1 character) (at least 1 item, each once). Optional.}\item{\code{field}}{A field by name: source "obs" for a column of the cells, "var" for a gene; key is the name as shown. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{key}}{The field or gene name as the app shows it. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{source}}{"obs" for a column of the cells, "var" for a gene. One of \code{"obs"}, \code{"var"}. Required.}}}\item{\code{max}}{For a continuous field or a gene: the largest value kept. A number. Optional.}\item{\code{min}}{For a continuous field or a gene: the least value kept. A number. Optional.}}}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{by}, \code{empty} (Categories of \code{by} left out for having no cells (none open, or none the view shows)), \code{field}, \code{groups}, \code{read_for} (For a gene read for a sample of the open cells: the cells its statistics are of), \code{values} (For a gene: its values as shown and analyzed (Data mapping \ifelse{latex}{<U+203A>}{›} Expression values, expression_transform_set): raw counts as stored, or the transform and where the cells' totals came from; null for an obs field), \code{within} (The cells kept by \code{within}: its field and how many open cells it keeps; null without it). Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
A continuous field or a gene per category of a categorical field (cells, mean, median, range, share above zero), or a categorical field's top categories per category.
}
